(K + M), where K is the eligible records kept and M those excluded, so a
recall target is a cap on M: with K eligible kept, recall T is met when M
is at most floor(K (1 - T) / T). Give that cap as \code{max_lost}, using a pilot
estimate of K, and the excluded frame's size as \code{frame_n}.

The exact size is the smallest n for which a frame holding \code{max_lost} + 1
eligible records would show none of them in a sample of n with probability
at most alpha, from the hypergeometric distribution. This is the bound
\code{\link[=gr_calibrate]{gr_calibrate()}} reports. The binomial version, n >= ln(alpha) / ln(1 - u)
with u = \code{max_lost} / \code{frame_n} (299 for u = 1\%), is given beside it; it
ignores the finite frame and so asks for a few more records.
